# text = Now when the high priest and the chief judge saw the hardness of his heart, yea, when they saw that he would revile even against God, they would not make any reply to his words; but they caused that he should be bound; and they delivered him up into the hands of the officers, and sent him to the land of Zarahemla, that he might be brought before Alma, and the chief judge who was governor over all the land.
# sent_id = 43
# llm_note = Complex sentence with two advcl when-clauses before main clause. Main verb chain: "they would not make" (T30–38) ; "but they caused" (parataxis/conj T40–47) ; "and they delivered...and sent" (conj T49–68) with purpose "that he might be brought before Alma...". "yea" = INTJ discourse on second 'saw'(21). "caused that he should be bound" = causative: 'caused' VERB, 'that'-clause ccomp. "delivered him up" = V+prt. "the chief judge who was governor" = second conj of Alma, with acl:relcl "who was governor over all the land".
